## 2. Standard Kapso WhatsApp webhook events

| Event | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `whatsapp.message.received` | A new WhatsApp message was received from a customer |
| `whatsapp.message.sent` | An outbound message was successfully sent to WhatsApp |
| `whatsapp.message.delivered` | An outbound message was delivered to the recipient’s device |
| `whatsapp.message.read` | The recipient read the outbound message |
| `whatsapp.message.failed` | The outbound message failed to deliver |
| `whatsapp.conversation.created` | A new WhatsApp conversation was initiated |
| `whatsapp.conversation.ended` | A conversation ended through closure or inactivity |
| `whatsapp.conversation.inactive` | No inbound or outbound messages occurred for the configured inactivity period |
| `whatsapp.contact.identity_changed` | A contact’s business-scoped identity changed |
| `whatsapp.contact.marketing_preference_changed` | A contact stopped or resumed marketing messages |

Kapso sends the event name in:

```http
X-Webhook-Event: whatsapp.message.received
```

For `whatsapp.message.received`, Kapso may send a batch envelope when buffering is enabled. Alo King should support both single-event and batch payloads.

